Notebook[{
Cell["The Black-Box Certification Map", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"70a5896a-2f7d-804a-bb9f-d60d5145d627"],

Cell["\<\
Objective O3 \[LongDash] the indistinguishability boundary, from existing \
findings\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"3f59e219-2c0d-6942-b193-8cf20bbea6f8"],

Cell["\<\
The central question (O3): given only black-box access, under what conditions \
is it mathematically impossible to distinguish a genuine quantum device from \
a classical optical emulation at the input-output level? This notebook \
assembles the answer, so far, as a map. Every cell is grounded in a project \
finding (ledger key shown); open cells are marked open.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aac0d1a1-340c-e744-b8ae-ea7258ded648"],

Cell["\<\
1.  The correlation-lens staircase (access model \[Times] adversary strength)\
\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2a81876f-2693-c54a-b4c6-9c06968f4d33"],

Cell["\<\
Rows = how much access the tester has. Columns = how strong the classical \
emulator is. A cell says whether genuine quantum can be told apart from that \
emulator under that access.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bccdc247-f590-204f-bbdc-3911660e9be0"],

