Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     ItemBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"OPEN CELLS \[LongDash] where the map is not yet drawn\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       LineColor->RGBColor[0.42, 0.42, 0.5],
       FrontFaceColor->RGBColor[0.42, 0.42, 0.5],
       BackFaceColor->RGBColor[0.42, 0.42, 0.5],
       GraphicsColor->RGBColor[0.42, 0.42, 0.5],
       FontSize->11,
       FontWeight->Bold,
       FontColor->RGBColor[0.42, 0.42, 0.5]],
      ImageMargins -> 5,
      Alignment->Left,
      Background->RGBColor[0.9, 0.9, 0.92],
      StripOnInput->False]},
    {
     ItemBox[
      InterpretationBox[Cell["\<\
\[Bullet]  ADVERSARY-CLASS MAXIMALITY (H4'): Prop O3-C (2026-07-13) proves \
the gate set {C1-C5, G7, G7-CV, G8} COMPLETE within the intensity-emulator \
class A_IE (KBS detector premise + white-box trust); devices OUTSIDE A_IE \
(photon-number resolution, heralded sources, non-fair-sampling) are the \
remaining frontier.
\[Bullet]  CONTINUOUS-VARIABLE column: FILLED 2026-07-13 by G7-CV, the \
Sp(2n,R) leaf-confinement audit (passive u(n) vs active sp(2n,R); \
exact-validated); same trust assumption as G7.
\[Bullet]  SAMPLING-HARDNESS caveat: poly-DLA \[DoubleLongRightArrow] \
efficient emulation only for algebra-supported observables; it does NOT \
preclude sampling hardness (Aaronson-Arkhipov). A distinct axis the map does \
not yet resolve.
\[Bullet]  cct-optimality sits INSIDE the mesh testbed for the resource axis \
\[LongDash] it is off this map (a cell-interior detail, not a boundary).\
\>",ExpressionUUID->"bf158912-ba58-c149-932f-2c8b44205b95"],
       TextCell[
       "\[Bullet]  ADVERSARY-CLASS MAXIMALITY (H4'): Prop O3-C (2026-07-13) \
proves the gate set {C1-C5, G7, G7-CV, G8} COMPLETE within the \
intensity-emulator class A_IE (KBS detector premise + white-box trust); \
devices OUTSIDE A_IE (photon-number resolution, heralded sources, \
non-fair-sampling) are the remaining frontier.\n\[Bullet]  \
CONTINUOUS-VARIABLE column: FILLED 2026-07-13 by G7-CV, the Sp(2n,R) \
leaf-confinement audit (passive u(n) vs active sp(2n,R); exact-validated); \
same trust assumption as G7.\n\[Bullet]  SAMPLING-HARDNESS caveat: poly-DLA \
\[DoubleLongRightArrow] efficient emulation only for algebra-supported \
observables; it does NOT preclude sampling hardness (Aaronson-Arkhipov). A \
distinct axis the map does not yet resolve.\n\[Bullet]  cct-optimality sits \
INSIDE the mesh testbed for the resource axis \[LongDash] it is off this map \
(a cell-interior detail, not a boundary)."]],
      ImageMargins -> 8,
